## Performance: example-mix against https://cdr.example/openehr/v1

| | |
|---|---|
| target | https://cdr.example/openehr/v1 (example-cdr 2.4.0) |
| environment | example 8-vCPU VM, 8 cores, 8 GiB, NVMe storage, single node |
| host | no prescription claimed; generator on x86_64 linux, 8 threads, Example CPU @ 3.0GHz |
| workload | example-mix v1, custom: a document the instrument does not pin |
| digest | `sha256:b819e2e11c055b4440addfd14b486a1e11d338721da22f5a3a5dab1f4d53aa6a` |
| corpus | scale S: 100,000 EHRs, 1,000,000 compositions, seeded by this run |
| scout | knee estimate 200.9/s, from scout window 15 |
| noise | 1 pass; between-run noise unmeasured, no A/A floor attached |
| scope | A run of at most ten minutes measures steady-state capacity and says nothing about memory growth, data growth or behaviour over hours. |

### Plateaus

| | offered/s | achieved/s | p50 ms | p95 ms | p99 ms | p99.9 ms | max ms | errors | steadiness |
|---|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|---|
| ✓ | 100.4 | 100.4 | 7.9 | 41.7 | 100 | n/r | 615 | 0.00% | steady |
| ✓ | 150.6 | 150.6 | 8.1 | 44.1 | 125 | n/r | 750 | 0.00% | steady |
| ✓ | 180.8 | 180.7 | 15.7 | 232 | 795 | n/r | 12,091 | 0.00% | **unsteady** |
| ✕ | 210.9 | 210.3 | 16.0 | 2,370 | 7,246 | n/r | 30,015 | 0.22% | steady |

✓ qualifies, ✕ fails. n/r: not resolvable, fewer than 10 samples lie above the quantile. Unsteady: the second half's p50 or p95 over the first's lies outside 0.8 to 1.25.

