### Server readings

Context only: no reading bears on a plateau's qualification.

- Database settings: PostgreSQL 18.6; shared_buffers 262144 8kB, work_mem 16384 kB, effective_cache_size 524288 8kB, max_connections 200, jit off

| offered/s | containers | database growth |
|--:|---|--:|
| 100.4 | sut cpu 31% (max 32%), rss 636 MB; db cpu 18% (max 19%), rss 1.4 GB | +7.8 MB |
| 150.6 | sut cpu 46% (max 48%), rss 628 MB; db cpu 27% (max 28%), rss 1.4 GB | +7.9 MB |
| 180.8 | sut cpu 55% (max 58%), rss 626 MB; db cpu 32% (max 34%), rss 1.4 GB | +8.4 MB |
| 210.9 | sut cpu 64% (max 67%), rss 626 MB; db cpu 37% (max 39%), rss 1.4 GB, truncated | +9.8 MB |

Costliest statements at the knee:

- 28,532 ms, 54 calls: SELECT count(*) FROM ehr.comp_data c WHERE c.archetype_id = $1
- 7,262 ms, 1,356 calls: INSERT INTO ehr.comp_data (id, ehr_id, data) VALUES ($1, $2, $3)
- 833 ms, 3,471 calls: SELECT e.id, e.created FROM ehr.ehr e WHERE e.id = $1
